Thanks [~accountid:5f9197f8606d4000694ceed2] 😊  Noted on the issue tags. 

Feature is planned to be launched in February 2025.

----

To answer your questions:

{quote}Cashback BB will not go to the same place as refund BB. How will it look like for users? What info will be available in the app? Will there be two distinct “wallets”?{quote}

Is this true tho that the cashback will not go to the same place as refund BB? I understood that the cashback (and expiry dates etc) will be visible under Profile → Bolt Balance page (Alexander’s response to me and [this Figma design|https://www.figma.com/design/hTmBFTYdlynOcGtxFnHIbM/Eater---In-progress?node-id=77-57952&node-type=instance&t=vecT9wZAg9WidwwX-0]), it’s just some technical limitations that are restricting the refund being expiring as well. Let me know if this was not your question and let’s specify in channel 😄

{quote}* {color:#ff5630}Top up is triggered once the order state is delivered{color} with relevant bonus value based on final basket value. *I don’t understand this sentence I’m afraid, especially the part not in red*{quote}

Assuming that this means that the cashback is transferred to balance once the order has been delivered and “relevant bonus value based on the final basket value” refers to the amount of money. Some campaigns are not item specific but some % from the basket value. 

{quote}Re tech issues *- is my understanding correct that no CS investigation will be taking place? If Eaters contact CS about this particular issue, they just need to escalate to TS and TS will resolve it?*{quote}

Yes, the phrasing in doc is misleading. Issue resolutions are actually not passed to CS. CS only has to escalate to TS if the eater is contacting us about the unsuccessful top up.

{quote}Expiring cashback - *so this will be communicated when they get it + push notifications? Will it also say in the “wallet” - expires on X date or in X days?*{quote}

Yes, based on the Figma design (also linked above) eaters can check their expirations in the app. 

{quote}Don’t understand the part anout “burning”:

“Burn” relevant amount of money from Bolt Balance after expiration period following top-up date.{quote}

Perhaps worth confirming, but my understanding is: Remove the amount of money from their balance if it was expired and not used.

{quote}“Some part of their cashback is about to burn” - this is if they got multiple cashbacks with different expiration dates, or? 

Do we know if there is prioritisation if user has “regular” BB and cashback BB? Which one will apply to order first?{quote}

Yes, eaters have to be able to differentiate between their multiple cashbacks and also between regular balance and cashback. I don’t think the prioritisation is in place or if the eater can choose which one to use. [Based on this Figma section, |https://www.figma.com/design/hTmBFTYdlynOcGtxFnHIbM/Eater---In-progress?node-id=77-62031&node-type=instance&t=vecT9wZAg9WidwwX-0]it is under legal review.

----

If something seems suspicious let’s raise in channel 😊

