Hello [~accountid:5f7aaad6021acf0076d55a90] ! 

I looked into this with Legal and it was agreed that if the driver does not complete the trip with the right rider, he is not obligated for commission. 

We will amend the process as such: 

*In-app payment*

* Refund the full price of the ride to the rider’s original payment method with _Driver_ as the actor at fault.
* {color:#4c9aff}If not already provided, ask the driver if they eventually still completed the ride with the correct rider:{color}
 {color:#4c9aff}*Trip happened with the correct rider:*{color}{color:#4c9aff} Calculate the commission fee and manually compensate the driver.{color}
{color:#4c9aff} {color}{color:#4c9aff}*Trip happened with the wrong rider:*{color}{color:#4c9aff} Do not manually compensate the commission fee.{color}
* Inform the driver about the compensation and continue to Step 2.



*Step 2: Advise the driver*

* Advise the driver to always check the name of the passenger in their car and to not start the trip until the right rider is in the vehicle.
* {color:#4c9aff}Inform the driver that they will not receive any commission compensation for completing the trip incorrectly.{color}
* Leave a comment on the order page. No further action is necessary.

