*Update:* 

* Pavestones has shared suggestions to our Privacy Notice for Passengers. 
* Attaching the document below. [^Privacy Notice for Passengers - BOLT (04122024).docx] 

{color:#0747a6}*Overall, Pavestones suggests to tailor the Privacy Notice specifically for the Nigeria Market, by adding/adjusting the following:* {color}

* to change _Bolt Operation OU_ to {color:#bf2600}*_Bolt Support Nigeria Limited_* {color}in all sections where there is a reference to Bolt Operations OU
* In section 6 “_Does Bolt transfer your personal data to other countries?_ to amend: 
** European Economic Area (“EEA“) → {color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria_* {color}
** European Commission → {color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC)_*{color}
** link to the European Commission website → {color:#bf2600}*_link to the NDPC’s website_* {color}
** the EEA to → {color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria_* {color}in the part re/ SCCs “We will rely on SCCs when we transfer personal data we collect from -the EEA- {color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria_*{color} and the United Kingdom to the United States, Singapore and -Nigeria- {color:#bf2600}*_European Economic Area (“EEA“)_* {color}where some of our third party service providers are based. 
* the EEA to → {color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria_*  {color}in section 7  i.e. [… personal data collected in the course of providing Bolt services is transferred to and stored
in our data centres which are located within -the EEA-{color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria_*{color}.]
* in section file a complaint: Estonian Data Protection Inspectorate (“AKI“) to {color:#bf2600}*_Nigeria Data Protection Commission_* {color}
* In section 4 _What purposes do we use your personal data for and what is our legal basis for processing?_ -  they’ve added the word {color:#bf2600}_“relevant“ :_ {color}
_Performance of a Contract: When it is necessary for Bolt (or a third party) to process your personal data to provide you with the Bolt services we promised you and meet our obligations under the Terms and Conditions for Passengers. Where the legal basis for processing your personal data is performance of a contract, and you choose not to provide the_{color:#bf2600} *_relevant_*{color} _information, you may be unable to use the Bolt services._
* For one of the purposes of processing i.e. _To make sure that your journey goes smoothly_  - a new legal basis was added by Pavestones → {color:#bf2600}*_Performance of a contract_* {color}
* and some minor typos here and there 


[~accountid:63622ea17d4645af4f03bd18] , to conclude I think they’ve just changed all references from EEA to Nigeria in the Privacy Notice for Passengers, not sure we want to follow this advice and incorporate these changes, because if we do it might send a signal that we “localize” some of our policies which might send a “wrong message“ to Ghana, Kenya regulators ect. Happy to discuss on our next ODPO sync.

