_Is the technical vulnerability that allowed the fraudster to inject Complainant’s selfie and documents permanently patched? Please provide further explanations and evidence as to how such failures are currently prevented and on the basis of which Bolt has reached this conclusion._

{panel:bgColor=#ffebe6}
*Request hashing explained (high level)*

# Fraudster uploads an image → goes from SDK on mobile app to app store where it’s hashed
# Fraudster now injects another image → different image is received on our backend
# We recompute the hash (using the same method as in mobile app <> app store) in our backend
# ❌ the mobile app hash is different from the hash on our backend → {color:#bf2600}*image was injected*{color}
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
# User uploads an image → goes from SDK on mobile app to app store where it’s hashed
# Image and hash are received on our backend
# We recompute the hash received on our backend 
# ✅ the hash on mobile app and our backend are the same → {color:#006644}*the image was not injected*{color}
{panel}



*Hashing happens twice*. Once on the mobile app <> app store and second time on our backend. We basically compare the two hashes.

There are some nuances in the procedure, such as that there’s hashing between mobile app and app store, it creates some sort of intermediary hash but it’s not important to explain how the procedure works.



CC: [~accountid:712020:0c8dd65b-46d5-4dc0-b5bd-76209c1e8048]

+*STATUS*+

* *Deadline*: 24 December 2024
* *Request*: Rider originally asked for deletion of specific data. Now they are asking for deletion of their account, and an overview of data retained after deletion.
** Rider originally requested that we delete a ride and bad review.
*** “_This ride was cancelled, take a look at my GPS data in that moment. Othet people took It, and i received a bad review while not being on the car. At least remove the bad review please because it does not have anything to do with me_”. They then asked “Could you delete the ride? Because I don't feel responsable for something that did not happen”.
*** CS informed the rider “_The Rider Ratings feature allows drivers to make informed decisions about accepting or declining ride requests and exercise greater control over their work environment, as they can judge the average Rider Rating for a passenger based on ratings provided by other drivers before accepting a ride_.”
** On the same day, in light of CS response, rider asked “_I am asking for the permanent delete of my account, and on behalf of the EU GDPR law, you have to completely delete ALL of my data from your servers: my name, my email, and every other information related to me_.”
** Rider then followed this up with “_Could you please make a check about which data in particular you will have to retain after deletion_”.
* *Acknowledgement*: Sent on 24 November
* *Verification*: Confirmed (rider profile is [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/200684116/overview?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn])
* *Account*: Active
* *Tracker*: Registered in Cognito ([Link|https://www.cognitoforms.com/bolttechnologyo%C3%BC/datasubjectrightsrequeststracker/entries/1-all-entries/779])
* *Next* *Steps*:
** (1) Instruct CS to delete the account per the [usual process|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003841794?country=global&language=en].
*** i.e., Do checks and send [template|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/32264] reminding them that data will be unrecoverable, and asking them to confirm deletion request.
*** After 24 hours, archive the account. However, DO NOT SEND [account deletion confirmation|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/17964?country=global&language=en] - we will send this.
** (2) Double-check the data retained on the rider’s account (payment method should not be there) and adapt {color:#ff5630}the below{color} as necessary (see e.g., [+LSS-39507+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-39507]). 
*** [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] do you have any concerns with this revised draft? I have slightly adapted the example you provided on the basis that: (1) the below more closely aligns with the structure of the privacy notice; and (2) the user is not specifically asking about retention periods - just what data will be retained - so I do not recommend we get into retention periods unless pressed. LMKWYT.
** (3) Send the below response by 24 Dec.

----

Dear Roberto,

Thank you for your data subject rights requests, which we received on 24 November 2024. 

{color:#bf2600}-We respond to each request below.-{color}

{color:#bf2600}As a part of our commitment to ensure transparency in our data handling practices, we provide the following information in response to your request.{color}

*(1)* {color:#bf2600}*-Deletion of a bad review-*{color} {color:#bf2600}*Removal of a negative review left by a driver about you*{color}

{color:#bf2600}-Please note that unfortunately-{color} {color:#bf2600}We would like to point out {color}that {color:#bf2600}-we cannot-{color} {color:#bf2600}we are unable{color} to action this request. {color:#bf2600}We understand your request to delete specific data from your account. Unfortunately, our current system does not allow for the selective deletion of specific data points such a rating linked to a specific order.{color}

Your average rating is calculated based on the ratings provided by drivers over the previous 365-day period. Each of these ratings provided by drivers are inherently and unavoidably subjective, reflecting the personal experiences and perceptions of individual drivers rather than factual information. Bolt allows drivers to express opinions about riders through ratings to provide additional reassurance to drivers and to provide a safe and accountable marketplace environment. This in turn empowers drivers to make informed decisions about accepting or declining ride requests and exercise greater control over their working environment. It is therefore of utmost importance that these ratings are maintained on our platform in accordance with applicable laws. 

*(2) Deletion of your account* {color:#bf2600}*and data associated with it*{color}

Please note that your account {color:#bf2600}-has been-  {color}{color:#bf2600}was {color}deleted {color:#bf2600}on [DATE]{color} and the personal data linked to your profile {color:#bf2600}-has been- {color}{color:#bf2600}was {color}erased. 

However, {color:#bf2600}-please be aware-  {color}{color:#bf2600}we need to inform you {color}that certain personal data may be retained in accordance with the relevant data protection regulations, even after the account deletion. For details about the retention periods of your personal data, please refer to the below and to our privacy notice available at [https://bolt.eu/ro-ro/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/ro-ro/privacy/privacy-for-riders/?category=rides] .

*(3) Data retained after account deletion*

We set out below the retention rules that apply to the personal data we retain after you request to delete your account:

{color:#ff5630}*Profile data*{color}{color:#ff5630} that includes communication preferences and notification settings{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To demonstrate your consent and to know whether to send you any news and offers, and other notifications.{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services and to comply with applicable legal requirements{color}

{color:#ff5630}*Identification / verification data*{color}{color:#ff5630} that includes information extracted from your passport and driver license provided for the purposes of verification{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services, to comply with applicable legal requirements, and to respond to requests from government / law enforcement agencies{color}

{color:#ff5630}*App usage data*{color}{color:#ff5630} that includes last device log-in session, order history, device data and phone number{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To prevent, detect and investigate account abuse{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services, to comply with applicable legal requirements, and to respond to requests from government / law enforcement agencies{color}

{color:#ff5630}*Device data*{color}{color:#ff5630} that includes device name, app version, OS version, IP address{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To prevent, detect and investigate account abuse{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services, to comply with applicable legal requirements, and to respond to requests from government / law enforcement agencies{color}

{color:#ff5630}*Communication data*{color}{color:#ff5630} that includes communications with the Customer Support Team at Bolt{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To prevent, detect and investigate account and payment abuse{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To conduct research, testing and analysis to better understand and improve the quality of Bolt's services{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services, to comply with applicable legal requirements, and to respond to requests from government / law enforcement agencies{color}

{color:#ff5630}*Rider rating data* {color}{color:#ff5630}including your average rating{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630} {color}{color:#ff5630}For the accounts where you completed rides, we retain the average rating for the purposes of investigating safety incidents{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services, to comply with applicable legal requirements, and to respond to requests from government / law enforcement agencies{color}

{color:#ff5630}*Payment data*{color}{color:#ff5630} including your attempts to add payment methods to the app and your invoices for completed riders{color}

* {color:#ff5630}*_Purposes_*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To comply with applicable tax, accounting and financial reporting purposes{color}
** {color:#ff5630}To analyze and handle claims and disputes relating to the use of Bolt's services, to comply with applicable legal requirements, and to respond to requests from government / law enforcement agencies{color}

If you are dissatisfied with this response to your requests or in relation to any other matter relating to the processing of your personal data, we hope you will continue to work with us to resolve them. You also have the right to complain directly to your data protection authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy. If you have any further questions, please let us know.

Yours sincerely,

*Bolt*

