As for me, this is not a bug but rather a specific validation for the {{postWithArgs}} method. 

The difference is how the data provider works, for the {{post}} it returns just body, while for {{postWithArgs}} it returns {{{query: req.query, body: req.body}}};

Please consider this implementation as an example [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/009db2a87a95ac8c477c32890d041aaf6e040582/src/foundation/monitoring/alerting_forwarder/main/validator/PostWithArgsRequestValidator.ts#L8|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/009db2a87a95ac8c477c32890d041aaf6e040582/src/foundation/monitoring/alerting_forwarder/main/validator/PostWithArgsRequestValidator.ts#L8] 
It allows to avoid this body field. For instance, this is how validation error looks for the data field (no body property):

{noformat}{
  "error": "Validation error",
  "property": "data",
  "children": [
     {
       "error": "Not string",
       "property": "name"
     }
  ]
}{noformat}

