See above for marked up version from SGX and I’ve added commentary/context below as per their email to us. I’ve also added initial response from myself / action items for consideration from the team in {color:#36b37e}green{color} alongside  

The main points for consideration as follows:

# *Bolt Duties and Obligation:* Requesting to add a section for Bolt Duties and Obligations include but not limited to 1) Non engagement with SGX competitors for electric tricycle during the 2-year period. 2) Bolt KPI to ensure SGX riders can achieve their KPI.  
{color:#36b37e}1. We can’t do this for 2 reasons: (1)This would prevent us from onboarding anyone with a 3 wheeler or electric 3 wheeler, even if we don’t financially support them - which is ridiculous. (2) SGX can’t fill the need for our category plans in Nigeria alone - so it’s a firm no. {color}[~accountid:622852f26a4c4c0070b16e66]{color:#36b37e} {color}[~accountid:712020:7250d115-7c52-46bf-8d9f-1a48a1d58b25]{color:#36b37e} - aligned on #1? {color}
{color:#36b37e}2.. Seems like they want us to “guarantee demand” of their drivers receiving 120 orders per week. I don’t want to go down the road of an earnings guarantee. {color}[~accountid:712020:7250d115-7c52-46bf-8d9f-1a48a1d58b25]{color:#36b37e} {color}[~accountid:5ad49d416f41620ce1adf1ee]{color:#36b37e} are you comfortable of adding this clause in? {color}

# *Section 3.5 & 3.6:* SGX is requesting that the penalty and\or commission bonus be based on "Finished trips per week" KPI only since this links to revenue. Thus, Bolt should state the minimum trip request per week per driver to ensure SGX Rider can achieve the set finished trips per week.  {color:#36b37e}Will defer to  {color}[~accountid:712020:7250d115-7c52-46bf-8d9f-1a48a1d58b25]{color:#36b37e} {color}[~accountid:5ad49d416f41620ce1adf1ee]{color:#36b37e} - are you comfortable of adding this clause in? (Same point above){color}

# *Section 3.6:* Bolt to add a table for commission bonus. {color:#36b37e}Not sure we need a table, we just need to be specific - {color}[~accountid:5ad49d416f41620ce1adf1ee] {color:#36b37e}please deal with this.{color}

# *Section 5.2:* Requesting this section to include payment of pilot phase be based on proforma invoice from manufacturer/supplier in order to pay for the units so the manufacturer can ship the CKD parts before Jan 31. This proposed change captures our understanding that Pilot Fees will be paid in advance to enable orders for the vehicles to be placed, while Scale-Up fees will be paid after vehicles arrive at the territory. {color:#36b37e}I’m aligned with upfront payment for the pilot phase (for speed of execution), but I don’t want us to pay the supplier - would rather pay the fleet. So they can submit the usual irrevocable order AND the pro-forma invoice as supporting docs. WDYT {color}[~accountid:622852f26a4c4c0070b16e66] [~accountid:712020:7250d115-7c52-46bf-8d9f-1a48a1d58b25] 

# *Section 1: Definition - Vehicle Deployment City:* Requesting this definition be expanded to multiple cities for flexibility and growth. Also, SGX board wants the 1000 units across multiple cities. {color:#36b37e}Generally OK with this - I think we’d need 1,000 in Lagos as a very minimum but happy to be flexible. {color}[~accountid:712020:7250d115-7c52-46bf-8d9f-1a48a1d58b25] [~accountid:5ad49d416f41620ce1adf1ee]{color:#36b37e} are you happy?{color}

# Additional request to include in Bolt Duties and Obligations section: Bolt to promote and advertise an "Electric Tricycle" segment to the public to accelerate customer engagement via Bolt App. {color:#36b37e}Happy with this{color}


Other comments and notes are stated in the document.

