Hi [~accountid:62bff85c118b20bee2bdca35] / [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] - I wanted to flag a quick issue I have spotted on the Bulk DSARs that affects 4 of the 40 users to date. Hopefully this should be a relatively easy fix but I wanted to run it past GFT first before pushing ahead. Sam has already reviewed this.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*What is the issue?*
{panel}

* We include the following language in each of our responses to address each user's A22 concerns: "_Bolt may use automated processes for the purposes of fraud detection and prevention, detecting violations of our platform terms, and applying suspensions and blocks as needed. This includes in the context of suspending Bolt accounts on the grounds of expired documents. However, in compliance with applicable local laws and regulations, Bolt will not permanently block a driver’s account unless the decision has been subject to human review[_*_, and in any case your account is currently active and has not previously been the subject of any suspension or block_*_]."_ 
** The language in square brackets is included where we have reviewed the user's account and seen that it has not previously been suspended / blocked.
* I was doing an extra review of the users to whom we have sent responses so far, and noticed that *four users were previously the subject of a suspension / block* at some point (e.g., due to a safety case, low customer ratings etc.), but the responses include the language in square brackets. As such, the inclusion of this language in their responses is technically inaccurate.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*What is the solution?*
{panel}

* IMO, this only affects the language in square brackets, as the rest of the A22 statement till holds up. For each of the four users at-issue, the suspension / block was temporary and no longer applies (in most cases, it lasted no longer than one day). As such, I do not this this is especially damaging to our responses, but is still worth rectifying as we still do not know the context in which these DSAR responses will be used.
* I suggest we send the following to each of the four users to correct this error:

{quote}“_Please note that the statement in our previous response that your account "has not previously been the subject of any suspension or block” was included in error. You can find information on any previous suspensions / blocks applicable to your account in the data export provided with our previous response. Nevertheless we reiterate that, in compliance with applicable local laws and regulations, Bolt will not permanently block a driver’s account unless the decision has been subject to human review._"{quote}

